{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Eulerian number a(n, m) using dynamic programming.\n    It follows the recurrence a(n,m) = (n-m)a(n-1,m-1) + (m+1)a(n-1,m).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # 'prev_row' stores the Eulerian numbers for the (current_n - 1) row.\n    # It is initialized to effectively represent a(1,k) values for the first iteration (current_n = 2).\n    # a(1,0)=1, and a(1,m)=0 for m >= 1.\n    prev_row = [0] * n\n    prev_row[0] = 1\n\n    # Iterate from n=2 up to the target 'n'.\n    for current_n in range(2, n + 1):\n        # 'curr_row' will store the Eulerian numbers for the current 'n' value.\n        curr_row = [0] * current_n\n        for current_m in range(current_n):\n            # Calculate a(current_n, current_m) using the recurrence relation.\n            # a(n,m) = (n - m) * a(n - 1, m - 1) + (m + 1) * a(n - 1, m)\n            term1 = (current_n - current_m) * (prev_row[current_m - 1] if current_m - 1 >= 0 and current_m - 1 < len(prev_row) else 0)\n            term2 = (current_m + 1) * (prev_row[current_m] if current_m < len(prev_row) else 0)\n            curr_row[current_m] = term1 + term2\n        prev_row = curr_row\n\n    # After the loop, 'prev_row' contains the Eulerian numbers for the target 'n'.\n    return prev_row[m]"}
