{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "from typing import Optional, Any\n\nclass EvenBitsError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for evenbits library errors.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        self.message = message\n        super().__init__(self.message)\n\nclass InvalidInputError(EvenBitsError):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input values.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, field: str, value: Any):\n        self.field = field\n        self.value = value\n        message = f\"Invalid input for {field}: {value}\"\n        super().__init__(message)\n\ndef validate_non_negative_int(value: Any, name: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Ensures value is an int and non-negative; raises InvalidInputError otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, int) or value < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(name, value)\n    return value\n\ndef default_width_for(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Returns the default width for a number, which is max(1, n.bit_length()).\"\"\"\n    return max(1, n.bit_length())\n\nclass BitMaskFactory:\n    \"\"\"Factory for creating bit masks based on specified width.\"\"\"\n    def create_even_mask(self, width: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns an integer mask with 0-based odd indices (1-based even positions) set up to width.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if the width is not positive.\n        \"\"\"\n        if width <= 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"width\", width)\n        mask = 0\n        for i in range(width):\n            if i % 2 == 1: # 0-based odd indices correspond to 1-based even positions\n                mask |= (1 << i)\n        return mask\n\ndef even_bit_set_number(n: int, width: Optional[int] = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-numbered bits (1-based position) of a given non-negative number.\n    It computes a mask for the specified or default width and then performs a bitwise OR.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = validate_non_negative_int(n, \"n\")\n\n    current_width = width\n    if current_width is None:\n        current_width = default_width_for(n)\n    \n    current_width = validate_non_negative_int(current_width, \"width\")\n\n    mask_factory = BitMaskFactory()\n    mask = mask_factory.create_even_mask(current_width)\n    \n    return n | mask"}
