{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next perfect square strictly greater than a given number n.\n    Handles negative inputs by returning 0 if 0 is greater than n.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        if 0 > n: # 0 is the smallest non-negative perfect square\n            return 0\n    \n    # Calculate the integer square root (floor) of n\n    # For n = 35, root = 5\n    # For n = 36, root = 6\n    root = math.isqrt(n)\n\n    # If n itself is a perfect square, we need the square of (root + 1)\n    # e.g., for n = 36, root = 6, we need (6+1)^2 = 49\n    # If n is not a perfect square, we still need the square of (root + 1)\n    # e.g., for n = 35, root = 5, we need (5+1)^2 = 36\n    return (root + 1) ** 2"}
