{"task_id": "Mbpp/472", "solution": "def check_Consecutive(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given list contains consecutive numbers.\n    Consecutive means the unique, sorted numbers form an arithmetic progression with a step of 1, and no duplicates are present.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Check for duplicates first, as per design. Duplicates make it non-consecutive.\n    if len(set(numbers)) != len(numbers):\n        return False\n\n    # Sort the numbers to check for a consecutive sequence\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    # A consecutive sequence of unique numbers will have max - min equal to (count - 1)\n    return (sorted_numbers[-1] - sorted_numbers[0]) == (len(sorted_numbers) - 1)"}
